<!--
F1 1984 for F-Retro_Gen3, on the TAMS2SP 1983 skinpack.

The skinpack adds 24 liveries, and every 1984 driver but two sits in the 1983 livery of the
team they drove for (livery_name must stay as the pack spells it). The other two, RAM, race the
BT52's stock white cars (livery IDs 53/54). AMS2 does not apply a Custom AI entry to those under
their shown names ("Brabham BT52 #5/#6"), so the pack's manifest is extended to rename them
"RAM-Hart #9 Alliot" / "RAM-Hart #10 Palmer". That manifest edit is NOT part of the pack:
  brabham_bt52.xml           beside this file: the edited manifest, copy it to
                             Vehicles\Textures\CustomLiveries\Overrides\brabham_bt52\
  brabham_bt52.original.xml  the pack's own, to undo it
Reinstalling or updating the skinpack overwrites the edit; without it the RAM entries never
match and those two cars race as AMS2's default AI. Models:
  formula_retro_g3 (V8)       Williams, Tyrrell #3/#4, Lotus #12, Ligier, Arrows, Theodore #34
  formula_retro_g3_te (turbo) ATS, Lotus #11, Renault, Alfa Romeo, Ferrari, Toleman #35, Spirit #40
  brabham_bt52                Brabham, RAM   mclaren_mp4_1c   McLaren

Seat mapping (1984 number in brackets):
  Brabham #5/#6   Piquet [1], Teo Fabi [2]          McLaren #7/#8   Prost [7], Lauda [8]
  Williams #1/#2  Rosberg [6], Laffite [5]          Tyrrell #3/#4   Brundle [3], Bellof [4]
  Lotus #11/#12   de Angelis [11], Mansell [12]     Renault #15/#16 Tambay [15], Warwick [16]
  Ferrari #27/#28 Alboreto [27], Arnoux [28]        Alfa #22/#23    Patrese [22], Cheever [23]
  Ligier #25/#26  Hesnault [25], de Cesaris [26]    Arrows #29/#30  Surer [17], Boutsen [18]
  ATS #9          Winkelhock [14]                   Toleman #35     Senna [19]
  Spirit #40      Baldi [21]                        Theodore #34    Ghinzani (Osella) [24]
  RAM #9/#10      Alliot [9], Palmer [10] (BT52 IDs 53/54)
1984 had 27 regular cars; this grid has 26. Tyrrell is kept in its own liveries although it
entered nothing after round 13 (Zandvoort), once FISA had excluded it from the season. Left out:
Toleman's second car #20 (Cecotto 1-10, absent 11-13, Martini/Johansson 14-16), the cars that
ran only part of the year, Osella #30 (Gartner, from round 10) and ATS #31 (Berger, four
rounds), and the drivers who stood in for single races. The pack's
#33 Guerrero and #36 Giacomelli liveries are commented out in its manifests, so they are not
used.

A livery's name carries its 1983 team, so an entry whose 1984 team differs says so in a
"team:" comment of its own (AMS2 ignores comments; ams2_career reads the team from them):
McLaren-TAG, Williams-Honda, Ligier-Renault, Arrows-BMW, Spirit-Hart, Osella-Alfa Romeo in
the Theodore livery, and Mansell's Lotus-Ford livery joins Lotus-Renault.

Car pace is set from the 1984 qualifying gap to pole (Rio, Zolder, Dijon, Brands Hatch,
Osterreichring, Monza): Brabham and McLaren ~0.1%, Lotus ~0.7%, Renault ~1.1%, Williams ~1.8%,
Ferrari ~2.5% (strong early, faded), Toleman (Senna) ~3.5%, ATS ~3.8%, Alfa ~4.2%, Ligier ~5.4%,
Arrows ~5.8%, Tyrrell ~6% (the only non-turbo team), Osella ~9%, RAM ~9.4%, Spirit ~9.5%.
The four car models have different base pace, so equal scalars do NOT mean equal speed:
the V8 models need much lower weight/drag than the turbo ones to keep up, and the turbo
model is slowed down so that McLaren (V8 model at its best scalars) can be at the front.
Race pace, reliability and the McLaren's dominance on Sunday come from the driver skills
and vehicle_reliability. power_scalar is kept within 0.90-1.00.
-->
